  "unresolvedCoverageGaps": [
    {
      "id": "grafana-gap-release-binding",
      "status": "open",
      "detail": "v13.2.3 source/docs are a candidate whole-product release. The studied npm artifact gitHead points at a source manifest labelled 13.2.2; a shipped complete OSS binary/client corresponding to this corpus has not been acquired or accepted."
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana-gap-semantic-review",
      "status": "open",
      "detail": "All 772 docs were mechanically scanned; none is claimed semantically complete. 34964 candidates still need splitting, deduplication, prerequisites, observables and edition/platform review."
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana-gap-edition",
      "status": "open",
      "detail": "An OSS label on a mixed OSS/Enterprise/Cloud document does not make every statement OSS. Paid/hosted headings are excluded as candidates; conditional/ambiguous paragraphs stay unresolved. Reporting, RBAC, SAML, SCIM, datasource permissions and other paid features must not be inferred from mixed overview examples."
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana-gap-rendered-includes",
      "status": "open",
      "detail": "Shared Markdown exists within this corpus, but Hugo shortcode expansion, inherited frontmatter, same-file shared blocks, refs resolution and exact rendered document structure have not been reproduced."
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana-gap-external",
      "status": "open",
      "detail": "External plugin documentation, linked tutorials, rolling Grafana Cloud docs, SDK/API-generated content, configuration source defaults and external query-language specifications are not exhaustively pinned by this 772-file corpus."
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana-gap-visual-code",
      "status": "open",
      "detail": "Screenshots, videos, play.grafana.org demos and arbitrary code-block examples are retained/referenced, but their extra feature details have not been extracted. The lexical scanner excludes code fences except selected formatting examples."
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana-gap-acceptance",
      "status": "open",
      "detail": "No contract in this inventory has been executed against a complete original Grafana instance. Local Metrics support and previous component evidence are not used to mark source requirements complete."
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana-gap-atomicity",
      "status": "open",
      "detail": "The authored contracts are bounded direct source behaviors/examples. Full input domains, error paths, limits, settings interactions, persistence/restart, accessibility and permission matrices remain to be normalized. Candidate counts are not feature counts."
    }
  ],
  "nextAction": "Review OSS-labelled and mixed-edition documents in bounded batches, first expand include/ref dependencies, then split/deduplicate candidates into observable contracts with original release/platform/edition acceptance fixtures. Preserve excluded paid/hosted material as boundaries."
}
# Grafana v13.2.3 documented OSS feature inventory — in progress

Pinned source: `6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e`. Acquisition covers all **772/772** catalogued Markdown files (**7,584,816 bytes**) with matching original Git blob SHA and SHA-256. All files are locally preserved under `work/grafana-inventory/corpus/`.

**This is not a complete semantic feature inventory.** All 772 files are mechanically scanned, with 9213 source sections and 34964 unreviewed candidate statements. Candidate counts do not count completed features. The artifact contains 104 authored/direct-definition/example contracts from 12 files; zero documents are marked semantically complete and zero original acceptance contracts have been executed.

