## Scope and edition/platform boundaries

The corpus includes OSS, Enterprise and Grafana Cloud documentation. Document labels provide a candidate scope, not an automatic statement-level license or availability decision. Paid/hosted section headings are separated from OSS candidates. Ambiguous restrictions remain unresolved. Reviewed atomic contracts preserve the exact source path, SHA, line span and any narrower boundary. No paid feature is inferred as available in OSS.

Windows, macOS, Debian/Ubuntu, RPM, Docker and Kubernetes sources retain their explicit platform context; unspecified behavior stays unclassified. Complete release/build correspondence remains unresolved.

